/// The upgrade of a running version 1 or 2 counter to version 3, as the
/// language stands: the running loop's mailbox type is
/// `Service.Envelope(Counter.Msg, Int)`, and the new loop's is
/// `Service.Envelope(Counter.Msg, Counter.Count)`, so the function the
/// `Upgrade` carries cannot run the new loop. This module is expected not to
/// compile; its diagnostic is the experiment's finding.
export fn upgrade(old : Service.Handle(Counter.Msg, Int)) : Unit with n =
    match old {
        Service.Handle(loop = loop) ->
            send(loop,
                 Service.Upgrade(next = fn(total) =
                                     Service.run(Counter.step, Counter.migrate(total))))
    }
